# Anthropic PBC
## The public record in charts

Built from commit `23a4bb63cc0f` with risk codebook **v0.2-draft** (DRAFT: wording awaits review).
Every number on these slides is read from a committed table at build time.

<span class="tag">Model labels come from two NLI witnesses; a label counts only when both score it ≥ 0.5. Labels are proposals, not hand-verified findings: there is no gold set yet.</span>

---

## The argument (edition v0 of the paper)

**Anthropic's charter is legally real and legally toothless.**

- §365(b) gives directors no duty to any person on account of a public-benefit interest
- The public the charter names cannot enforce it.

Edition v0 of the paper (`docs/anthropic-contrapunctus.md` at `1afb042`) rests on Anthropic's own filings. This deck looks outward at public data.

---

<!-- _class: chart -->

![w:900](deck/ai-risk-by-year.svg)

<div class="src">AI framed as a risk: 12.2% of 2026 S&P 500 calls (to 2026-11-04), against at most 0.6% in any year before 2023.</div>

---

<!-- _class: chart -->

![h:520](deck/risk-ranking-ttm.svg)

<div class="src">137 firms raised AI as a risk in the 12 months to 2026-11-04. Most named: Cybersecurity (40), Safety / ethics / misuse (31), Overspending / capex return (26).</div>

---

<!-- _class: chart -->

![h:520](deck/intent-ttm.svg)

<div class="src">Analysts ask how AI sells (21.2% of AI questions) far more than how its risk is controlled (0.8%). Question-intent codebook v0.1.</div>

---

<!-- _class: chart -->

![h:540](deck/dialogue-space.svg)

<div class="src">Safety and ethics: 10% of executives' AI-risk passages, 39% on Hacker News about Anthropic, 61% on Wikipedia. Cyber dominates HN's AI-security set (85%).</div>

---

<!-- _class: chart -->

![w:950](deck/cve-ai-credit.svg)

<div class="src">CVE credits name Claude on 370 CVEs and any AI system on 924 (2020-01 to 2026-10). That cannot confirm or refute "33,000+": not every flaw becomes a CVE, and credits need not name the tool.</div>

---

## What this deck does not show

- **No effect of Anthropic on any outcome.** Attention and counts only.
- **No gold set yet.** Witness precision is unmeasured.
- **Survivorship.** The earnings-call universe is today's S&P 500.
- **No news-attention chart.** GDELT's daily series omits days, so it is not used.
- **Draft codebook.** Wording of v0.2-draft awaits human review.

Sources, licences and rebuild commands: `DATASETS.md`. Build stamp: `deck/STAMP.json`.

